    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p23.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(R\\) denote the given ratio. By the sum-to-product identities, \\[ \\begin{aligned} R&=\\frac{\\sin10^\\circ+\\sin20^\\circ} {\\cos10^\\circ+\\cos20^\\circ},\\\\ R&=\\frac{2\\sin15^\\circ\\cos5^\\circ} {2\\cos15^\\circ\\cos5^\\circ}\\\\ &=\\tan15^\\circ. \\end{aligned} \\] Therefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Apply the sum-to-product identities to both numerator and denominator",
        "Both transformed sums contain the same \\(\\cos5^\\circ\\) factor"
      ],
